      "title": "AMP's $5.5B Buyback Aids Shareholder Returns: Will It Be Sustainable?",
      "summary": "Ameriprise Financial authorized an additional $5.5 billion for share repurchases through September 2028, supported by strong excess capital and free cash flow generation. The company returned $1.9 billion to shareholders in H1 2026 and has returned approximately $25 billion over the past decade. However, competing capital investments in technology, AI, and business expansion raise questions about long-term sustainability of the buyback program.",
